In article <5011@rhino.qpsx.oz.au>, marting@rhino.qpsx.oz.au (Martin Gregory)
says:
>
>I know that eating some poisonous creatures can give you poison
>resistance... does eating _any_ poisonous creature have this chance,
>or only some specific ones (in which case, which ones??).

I believe that all creatures that have poison Attacks can grant you
poison resistance (water moccasins, homunculi, killer bees).  There
are some other healthy critters that aren't poisonous (like spiders
and fungi).  However, not all poisonous corpses give you resistance
(like kobolds).

A good rule of thumb is that if your pet won't eat it, you probably
don't want to eat it.  Pets happily eat non-poisonous things, and
they avoid poisonous corpses.  It happens that they also avoid
eating fungi, but that's only because your pet is a Carnivore
and doesn't consider a mold to be a meat.

>Also, I've heard that tengus give teleport control.  But I'm lawful -
>how do I get a tengu corpse?  Just now I decided to have a go at a
>peaceful tengu for the heck of it.  The darn thing didn't leave a
>corpse anyway!!  Was this a bad move?

Attacking peaceful things is almost always a bad move, particularly
when they are co-aligned.  A couple Safe ways to get around this
problem is (1) let your pet kill the peaceful critter and (2)
don't be lawful.  (1) is a much better and more likely proposition.

